WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Zero kara kakedashite

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Start running from
the beginning,

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
Omoi dake
wo dakishimete

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
with nothing but your emotions
in your hands.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Sonomama kakenukete

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Just keep running...

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
Itsumo koko
de mitsumeteru

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
I'm always watching
you from here.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
Hajimete deatta hi no
manazashi wasurenai

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
I still remember your expression
the day we first met.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
Taiyou mitai ni kokoro
wo terashitekureta

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
It lit up my heart like the sun.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
Asu no yukue sagashite
nayandeiru nara

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
If you're anxious about
where to go tomorrow,

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
Ima kimi no tame
ni akari ni naritai yo

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
I want to become
a beacon to you.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Zero kara tobidatte

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Start flying from
the beginning.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Ima no kimi
wo toki hanachi

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Let go of your current self...

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
Mugen ni habataite

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
and fly towards infinity.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
Donna toki
mo mimaru yo

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
I will always watch over you...

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
Kitto zutto tooku made

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
no matter how far you fly.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.080
Episode 46 - Into the
Valley of Plums

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.590
So, the time to leave
has finally arrived.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.880
What a coincidence.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:54.110
I just got back from a business
trip on the previous bullet train.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:58.370
I'm expecting a beautiful Scarlet
Angel from you, you know.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:01.850
Thank you very much,
President Hayami.

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:07.610
Little one, I think I can expect a
unique Scarlet Angel from you.

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:08.740
Good luck.

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:10.710
Mr. Hayami...

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:12.800
You're Mr. Purple Roses.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:18.660
I'm going to give
it my best shot!

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:23.800
After all, I want to show my Scarlet
Angel to Mr. Purple Roses!

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:27.280
I've wanted to all along,
Mr. Hayami!

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.870
I wish Mr. Purple Roses
could hear that.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:33.410
I'm sure he'd be touched.

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:37.710
Well then, Mr. Chairman. I
shall take my leave now.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.210
See you soon, little one.

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:42.880
That's not my name!

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.050
I'm an adult now!

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:48.690
You really are him, aren't
you? Mr. Purple Roses...

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:03.300
I can't believe this is actually
happening, Ms. Tsukikage.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.290
We left Tokyo seven
hours ago.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:15.210
Ma'am, I'm finally here!

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.510
I'm finally with you again!

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:25.190
So, this is the home of <i>The
Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:27.490
We've been awaiting
your arrival.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.490
Mr. Genzo?

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:40.460
Ichiren Ozaki wrote <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>
based on a legend passed down in this village.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:47.470
It's a story centered around an angel who
is protected by a dragon and an ogre,

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:52.210
and a story about a Buddhist carver
and his plum tree.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:55.220
I'd love to see the valley where
the scarlet plums grow.

00:03:55.910 --> 00:04:01.050
That's the temple where Ichiren
resided as a child.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.690
Is that where Ms. Tsukikage
is staying?

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:07.920
Yes. But she had business
to take care of in town,

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.800
and she probably won't be back
before tomorrow morning.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:44.910
This is strange.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:51.050
I wonder where Ayumi and Genzo have
disappeared so early in the morning.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.270
That's...

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:24.270
It's the Scarlet Angel!

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:49.910
The wind...

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:53.750
No, there's no wind today.

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:04.440
It doesn't feel human...

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:05.760
How can that be right?

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:18.880
Welcome to the home of
<i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:20.250
Ms. Tsukikage!

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:24.770
So, this is the valley where
the scarlet plums grow.

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:26.400
Ma'am!

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:27.760
Ayumi.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:31.030
Seeing you like this brings
back memories.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.280
Mr. Chairman!

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.850
I thought I might
find you here.

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:38.030
I followed the sound of the
hand-drum.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:39.200
So did I.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.500
It's good to see you all again.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:47.010
Ma'am, I've finally made it to the home
of <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>!

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:49.050
Maya.

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:54.540
You don't know how happy it makes me to meet
you in the home of <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:56.570
Thank you, Ayumi.

00:06:57.470 --> 00:07:01.830
So, this is the scarlet plum tree that is rumored
to contain the mysterious Scarlet Angel.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:03.990
It's magnificent.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:06.780
I can't even guess its age,
but it must be pretty old.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:08.590
It truly is a holy tree.

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:12.350
It's probably a different tree from the one
the Buddhist carver Isshin worked with,

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:16.810
but it was the vision of this tree that Ichiren had in
mind when he wrote <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.540
This valley is a place
of mystery.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:23.410
The plum trees stay in bloom here
for six months every year.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:26.350
It's as if the seasons
are caught in time.

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.750
I've performed this role dozens of times, and
yet, every time I rehearse in this valley,

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:33.850
I still learn something new
about her character.

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:38.290
I feel like the feeling of perfection
will forever elude me.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:45.190
Ayumi. Maya. You both have
your own Scarlet Angels.

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:47.640
You are free to perform
to your heart's content.

00:07:48.010 --> 00:07:51.750
I have dreamed of the day you
will tutor me for so long.

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:53.450
Thank you so much.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.760
I'm going to become the
spirit of the plum tree!

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:59.320
Just the thought
of it excites me!

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:01.030
You're excited?

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:04.390
Here I am, wracked
with nerves...

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:06.520
This is the Scarlet Angel
we're talking about!

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:09.010
This is the role most actresses
can only dream of!

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:12.290
How is it possible for you to turn
it into... an exciting experience?

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:16.550
I'll tell you two a bit about
the Scarlet Angel.

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:21.320
Long, long ago, when this country
was torn apart by conflict,

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:26.720
the emperor wished for peace and commissioned
a Buddhist carver to sculpt an icon of an angel.

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:30.810
The carver was unsatisfied with everything
he produced, no matter what he carved.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.600
Then, someone gave the agonized
carver a piece of advice.

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:37.010
This person told him that there was a place where a 
sacredtree grew into a plum tree 
that was a thousand years old.

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:39.180
This person told him that, if he carved the
image of an angel into wood from that tree,

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:42.520
it would house the very spirit itself and
become an awe-inspiring sculpture.

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:46.000
The carver went on a pilgrimage to
find the tree the man talked about...

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:51.210
and met the spirit of the thousand-year-old
plum tree.

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:56.510
The first thing you must learn is what
the Scarlet Angel actually is.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:57.520
You got that?

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:58.300
Yes!

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:01.800
All right. I would like both of you
to turn into a plum tree now.

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:03.800
A plum tree?

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:04.810
Go!

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:35.000
I've kept this pose for so
long... my body aches.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.790
If I were a real tree, that
wouldn't happen.

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:47.190
That girl... she looks
so natural!

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:50.640
And relax!

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:52.990
What did you think,
Mr. Director!

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:58.720
Well, Ayumi's tree was very beautiful, but
because the pose was hard to hold,

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:01.510
she couldn't maintain it over
a long period of time.

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:09.000
Maya's pose was very simple, but the more time
passed, the more she looked like a real tree.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:13.270
But, on stage, you would never be
asked to hold a pose for so long.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:18.710
Which means that Ayumi's tree was
a better depiction of visual acting.

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:22.250
Visual acting... Ayumi,
you're amazing.

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:25.960
The more time passed, the more
she looked like a real tree.

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:28.640
Maya, you scare me.

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:34.550
Now, I'm going to ask
you both a question.

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:36.650
What would you find
under a tree?

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:39.850
Soil.

00:10:39.850 --> 00:10:43.720
And how does a tree get
nutrients from the soil?

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:47.030
By sucking up water
from the ground!

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:49.410
And how does that water
get into the ground?

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:52.520
Rain and dew soak
down into the earth.

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:56.140
And what else is necessary
for a plant to grow?

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:58.170
Sunlight!

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.170
The sun!

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:02.180
The steps to creating the Scarlet
Angel are as follows:

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:07.730
Wind, earth, water and fire. If you do
not understand these four elements,

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:10.390
you cannot hope to portray
the Scarlet Angel!

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:13.500
Lesson One: the wind!

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:15.510
How do you express
the concept of wind?

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.840
I want you to think about how you
would act out the wind blowing!

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:32.640
Right now, the wind is buffeting
my lower back...

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.970
It's blowing my hair...

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:36.600
How do you act out wind?

00:11:40.030 --> 00:11:41.930
The wind's shape.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:03.480
If you don't fan it, the fire
won't burn properly.

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:04.410
Yes, sir!

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:06.740
You fan the wind...

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:10.480
Fanning!

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:31.960
What are you planning,
Masumi?

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:36.240
The National Acting Association took
<i>The Scarlet Angel</i> from us,

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:38.530
and yet you just sit there
with a calm expression.

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:42.630
Ah, I see now. It's all going according
to your plan, isn't it?

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:45.760
When the committee get around to choosing
a venue for the performance,

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:49.460
it'll be Daito's stage
they pick, won't it?

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:52.550
I'm sure that'll be the
outcome, yes.

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:56.800
You've become quite
the tactician.

00:12:56.800 --> 00:13:01.090
By the way, I wanted to
talk to you about Shiori.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:04.860
Lesson One: I want you
to depict the wind.

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:08.780
All right. I'll go first.

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:18.020
She's just standing there.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:43.000
A breeze just blew across
the nape of her neck.

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:48.030
I can feel it, even though she
barely moved her shoulder.

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:52.030
That's enough. Wonderful.

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:56.500
By standing still at the beginning, you
drew attention to your next movement.

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:58.540
Even though your neck
movement was minute,

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:01.660
it drew the audience's eye
to that exact point.

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:05.620
The wind blowing across your neck; the slight
movement of your neck and your hands;

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:07.430
the faintest expression
on your face.

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:10.000
Your acting showed no
excess of movement.

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:12.480
Thank you very much.

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:14.130
Why did you choose
to depict it like that?

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:19.280
Because the wind has no shape,
but you can observe its form.

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:24.800
You can see the form of the wind
in the things that it moves.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:26.900
The leaves on a tree and
the petals of a flower...

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:31.520
I realized that, even in the tiniest of movements,
you can see the form of the wind.

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:35.600
It was like watching a perfected
Noh performance.

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:37.420
It really was wonderful.

00:14:39.550 --> 00:14:42.310
Next: Maya Kitajima.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:46.090
Now it's my turn.

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:47.390
My wind!

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.990
Is this a whirlwind?

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:18.290
That's a light breeze...
That's a headwind...

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:20.370
That's a tailwind...

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:30.920
Right, I'd like you to explain
your movements just now.

00:15:32.020 --> 00:15:36.680
Okay! The wind is born, and as it changes
form, it grows bigger and bigger...

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:39.620
until it finally dies again...

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:45.770
Maya! I told you to act out the
wind, not to become the wind!

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:49.710
If you're an actor, you
must learn to act!

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:54.110
For whose sake, you ask? For
the sake of the audience!

00:15:54.110 --> 00:15:56.600
Without an audience,
you cannot act!

00:15:57.070 --> 00:16:00.030
Even though becoming your role
might seem amazing to you,

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:02.640
there's a huge drawback
to what you're doing!

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:06.470
You are forgetting that
you are acting.

00:16:06.470 --> 00:16:10.550
And a person who has forgotten that
they are acting is not an actor!

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:13.190
Ayumi acted out the wind,
therefore she's an actress.

00:16:13.190 --> 00:16:16.880
You, however, are a failure.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:19.130
Yes.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:25.340
Scary. It's like she goes right to
the heart of a role immediately.

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:28.850
Right. Your next assignment
is fire.

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:32.830
Fire.

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:35.850
I don't get it.

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:40.080
I don't understand what acting
out wind, fire, water and earth,

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:42.780
has to do with the Scarlet
Angel herself.

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:54.750
Fire has movement.
Fire has rhythm.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:09.140
Ichiren... These two girls are trying
hard to inherit your soul.

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:15.340
Please give me the strength
to train your Scarlet Angel.

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:18.390
Just give me a little more
strength so I can live!

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:22.140
They told me to fetch
her medicine...

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:26.000
I guess that means she still
needs to go to the hospital.

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:33.690
What's Mr. Hijiri doing here?

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:42.630
Excuse me!

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:50.520
I didn't realize you were in the hospital
until the day we came to the village.

00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:54.220
But, what was Mr.
Hijiri doing here?

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:56.730
Soon, we'll be in the
Valley of the Plums.

00:17:57.320 --> 00:17:58.740
But that's...

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:00.680
Hey! Stop the car!

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:07.180
I see. So, you've finally started rehearsing
for <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:12.680
Yes. But I can't believe we randomly
met here like this!

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:18.170
I'm on my way to a hot spring nearby. And
where's the performance to be held?

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:25.750
I don't know yet. But if I'm picked for the role,
I don't want to act in the Daito Theater.

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:28.700
And why's that exactly? Don't
you like that stage?

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:32.160
No, I don't! I mean, well...

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:37.160
I suppose that's fine. I heard
their President's quite pushy.

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:40.370
You're right!

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:45.060
He's pushy, mean, overly
persistent and evil!

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:47.510
I hate that stuck-up
Masumi Hayami!

00:18:47.510 --> 00:18:49.140
I'd like to see what kind of parents
he has!

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:59.400
But how are the rehearsals
going with Ms. Tsukikage?

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:01.100
They're difficult.

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:04.680
For my next task, I'm supposed to act out
fire, but I still don't know how I should do it.

00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:11.470
Fire? Have you heard of the
play <i>Yaoya Oshichi</i>?

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:14.200
When a fire breaks out in Edo, Oshichi,

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:16.790
the daughter of a greengrocer,
meets an apprentice at the temple called Kichiza...

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:20.080
at a shelter and falls
in love with him.

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:24.940
Even after the fire has been extinguished,
she can't help but want to see him again,

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:27.020
and finally ends up
committing arson.

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:32.760
In that era, there was a
death penalty on arson.

00:19:33.140 --> 00:19:36.910
Even so, Oshichi thought she could
see Kichiza again if she started a fire.

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:40.580
The fire inside her heart ended
up consuming her.

00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:42.750
<i>Yaoya Oshichi</i>.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:50.210
Here's the play,
<i>Yaoya Oshichi</i>.

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:57.340
Isn't Miss Shiori upset that she still hasn't
heard a response from you, Mr. Masumi?

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:59.840
You don't miss a
trick, do you?

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:03.800
Do you love her? Miss
Shiori, I mean.

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:05.360
I do.

00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:08.140
And what do you plan on doing
with your purple roses then?!

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:15.690
The purple roses will never wilt in my
heart. No matter what happens.

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:18.630
No matter what happens...

00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:28.460
Miss Shiori...

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:30.600
No, don't come in here!

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:34.310
I don't need your pity!

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:36.420
Why did you agree to this
arranged marriage?

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:39.350
Why did you take me out, entertain
me and make me feel wanted?

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:43.060
Why? Why did you do that when
I haven't captured your heart?!

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:48.150
Why did you come here?

00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:51.140
Did you come here with those flowers,
picked out by your secretary,

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:54.400
as if you were visiting
a business partner?

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:59.120
I've hated meetings like these
ever since I was a child!

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:02.730
I picked out these
flowers myself.

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:06.770
And I came here today to give
you an official response.

00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:17.010
<i>Yaoya Oshichi</i>.

00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:23.230
I want to see Kichiza! No matter
what crime I have to commit!

00:21:23.230 --> 00:21:27.020
Kichiza! The fire in
Oshichi's heart.

00:21:27.020 --> 00:21:28.870
This is quite something.

00:21:30.020 --> 00:21:33.090
I don't think I've ever watched
fire burn so intently.

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:36.620
From moment to moment, no
single movement is the same.

00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:40.120
Her fire is like a dancer
with red shoes...

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:43.620
It dances until the
day it dies...

00:21:43.620 --> 00:21:46.460
The love of the
Scarlet Angel...

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:48.520
Love!

00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:56.680
Hello hello

00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:56.680
Hello, hello.

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:15.280
Fukanou dato iwarenagara
tobitatte

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:15.280
Even though they say it's
impossible, I fly off.

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:25.160
Kanaeta yume mo koboreochita
yume mo aru

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:25.160
There are dreams that come true,
and dreams that crumble away.

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:36.830
Soredemo isshoukenmei ikiru
kazu dake hoshi ga fueru

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:36.830
But even then, for every person trying hard
to live their life, a new star is born.

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:49.240
Kyou mo mata hitotsu
umareru hoshi miagete

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:49.240
Today, I look up again, at
another newly born star.

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:50.570
And I say,

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:50.570
And I say,

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:53.890
Hello hello another star

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:53.890
Hello, hello another star.

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:57.030
If I wish anything
will change

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:57.030
If I wish anything will change.

00:22:57.030 --> 00:23:02.770
Ai wo daite norikonda
shatoru

00:22:57.030 --> 00:23:02.770
I've boarded the shuttle
with my love.

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:09.120
Daremo ga hitori no
uchuuhikoushi dayo

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:09.120
Every single person
is an astronaut.

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:14.190
Negau yume
kara yume e

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:14.190
From fulfilled dream to dream,

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:21.470
Dokomademo
yukeru one life

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:21.470
I can go anywhere... One life.

00:23:22.650 --> 00:23:25.840
How can someone express
fire, I wonder?

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:29.640
You can't touch it or grab it
and it never stops moving.

00:23:29.640 --> 00:23:32.520
Watching it though,
it's so beautiful.

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:36.790
You show the fire very beautifully
with your dance, Ayumi.

00:23:36.790 --> 00:23:40.030
My fire. The fire of
Oshichi's love.

00:23:40.030 --> 00:23:43.970
The flames that burned down the city
of Edo with flames yearning for love.

00:23:43.970 --> 00:23:45.620
My love!

00:23:45.620 --> 00:23:50.130
When I think about it, he's
always been with me.

00:23:45.790 --> 00:23:51.580
Episode 47 - The
Flames of Love
